  "question": {
    "text": "In an experiment, brass and steel wires of length <math><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> each with areas of cross section <math><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> are used. The wires are connected in series and one end of the combined wire is connected to a rigid support and other end is subjected to elongation. The stress required to produce a net elongation of <math><mn>0.2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is,<br />[Given, the Young&#39;s Modulus for steel and brass are, respectively, <math><mn>120</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></math> and <math><mn>60</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></math> ]",
